Package: patchASR
Title: Patch-Based Ancestral State Reconstruction Across Branch-Localized Changes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(
      given = "Yuqi",
      family = "Cheng",
      email = "dreabder@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Implements patch-aware ancestral state reconstruction for
    continuous traits on rooted, fully bifurcating phylogenetic trees with
    one or more specified branch-localized shifts. Compatible non-overlapping
    shift regions are partitioned into mother and patch components, and a
    user-supplied ancestral-state reconstruction function is applied to
    eligible components. Boundary ancestral states are reconstructed using
    branch lengths from the original phylogeny, after which component and
    boundary estimates are merged back onto the internal nodes of the
    original tree while preserving node identity and estimate provenance.
URL: https://github.com/Dreabder/patchASR
